The Multi-Region Ocean Data Comparison Tool has been successfully developed and safely pushed to the repository. The code is isolated in the Camparisionfeature branch, meaning your main and fix/backend-connection branches remain entirely untouched and safe.

1. Architecture & Implementation Details
To build the side-by-side data comparison system, we added the feature using a modular, decoupled approach so it would not interfere with the existing 3D Globe logic.

🧩 Core Components
useComparisonStore.js: A brand new, standalone Zustand store. It manages the comparison state (open/close, active regions, selected floats, and API fetching) independently of the massive useOceanStore.js. It contains a robust bounding box dictionary of 29 worldwide ocean regions.
ComparisonWindow.jsx & .css: The main full-screen modal overlay. It uses a CSS flexbox layout (overflow-x: auto) that allows an infinite number of region panels to be stacked side-by-side. It features dark glassmorphism styling, backdrop blurs, and neon cyan accents to match the futuristic INCOIS dashboard.
RegionPanel.jsx: The individual column for a specific region. It contains:
Top Half: A debounced depth slider (0-4000m) and float selector dropdown.
Bottom Half: A real-time data table comparing Real Argo Telemetry with INCOIS-ROMS Model Data.
TopNavbar.jsx & OceanDashboard.jsx: We minimally modified these existing files to add the + Compare trigger button, the inline search bar, and to render the overlay on top of the 3D globe.
2. API Endpoints Integration
The comparison tool relies strictly on your existing Node.js/Express backend endpoints. We implemented intelligent data flow: when a user adds a region, the app fetches the regional fleet; when the user moves the depth slider, the app fetches the specific depth profile and model validation.

Feature Area	API Endpoint	Query Parameters	Description & Usage
Regional Fleet Discovery	GET /api/fleet	lat_min, lat_max, lon_min, lon_max	Uses the region's predefined bounding box to fetch all active Argo floats currently in that specific ocean area. Populates the float dropdown selector.
Real Argo Telemetry	GET /api/argo/depth-slice	platform_number, depth	Fetches the real-time, interpolated Temp, Salinity, O₂, Speed, and Chl-a for the selected float at the user's specific depth slider position.
Model vs Observation	GET /api/validation	platform_number, depth, lat, lon	Fetches the INCOIS-ROMS 1/12° model predictions and calculates the Delta variance against the real Argo data to determine bias (e.g. "Optimal Match", "Moderate Bias").
TIP

Performance Optimization: API calls to /api/argo/depth-slice and /api/validation are debounced by 300ms on the depth slider. This means the frontend waits until the user finishes sliding the depth bar before sending the request, preventing the backend and ERDDAP from being overwhelmed with hundreds of rapid requests.

